  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "service",
      "title": "Shared runtime",
      "items": [
        "dmserver and embedded bench scenarios share server/internal/runtime. The main listener requires TLS outside literal loopback. The optional separate HTTP-01 challenge listener may bind non-loopback plain HTTP.",
        "The application registers workers for supervision and readiness. A worker failure cancels sibling loops and reaches the runtime supervisor; shutdown follows the ordered HTTP drain path."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "service",
      "title": "Configured services and workers",
      "items": [
        "The unified application mounts administration, MDM and configured enrollment services. DDM uses the in-process adapter; public discovery, certificate routes and app notifications depend on configuration.",
        "Certificate renewal, native-webhook retention, persistent event delivery, DDM changes and DEP synchronization/assignment run under runtime supervision as configured."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "neutral",
      "title": "Ordered shutdown",
      "items": [
        "On shutdown, drain both HTTP listeners concurrently under one deadline, then cancel and await workers. Close clients, stores and application resources only when both HTTP and worker drains complete.",
        "An HTTP drain timeout force-closes connections but cannot prove handlers have exited. Return a failure while retaining shared resources and maintenance registration; stop the process before manually forgetting that participant.",
        "A worker failure may already have cancelled its siblings. Preserve the first failure, join any cleanup failure, and retain pending SQL deliveries."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "warning",
      "title": "Maintenance is a resumable pause",
      "items": [
        "Shared SQL maintenance admission wraps webhook observation and rate limits. A pause cancels workers and awaits admitted HTTP work, including deferred observation/capture writes, before acknowledging.",
        "New requests receive 503 during the pause or a control-store failure. The fence persists across timeout and restart; only the matching ownership ticket resumes work. Every registered writer must acknowledge."
      ]
    },
